We can use ALTER TABLE Commands to make alterations in the prepared table in follwoing ways: 


ADD: ALTER TABLE (table_name) add column (column_name) (datatype_column) value_youwant_toenter. 
  ALTER TABLE users
  ADD COLUMN is_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE;

MODIFY: Alter table (tablename) Modify column (column_name) datatype After Id    #if you want to put a coolumn after email column
  ALTER TABLE users
  MODIFY COLUMN name VARCHAR(150);

DROP: Drop is used to permanently drop(delete) table/column/data
  ALTER TABLE users
  DROP COLUMN is_active;

RENAME : Rename column name 
  ALTER TABLE users
  RENAME COLUMN phone TO mobile_number;


MOVE : To move a column to the first position 
  ALTER TABLE users
  MODIFY COLUMN email VARCHAR(100) FIRST;

Moving column name after another column
  ALTER TABLE users
  MODIFY COLUMN gender ENUM('Male', 'Female', 'Other')
  AFTER name;

Adding Multiple column :
  ALTER TABLE users
  ADD COLUMN phone VARCHAR(15),
  ADD COLUMN city VARCHAR(100);
